{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And you shall guard the matzot.</b> This means guard it from the time of harvest, that no water come upon it, and also guard it from the time of kneading, that it not become leavened. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: ״ושמרתם את המצות״ — read it as ״המצות״ (the commandments): just as one does not let matzah become leavened, so one does not let the commandments become leavened — if a commandment comes into your hand, do not let it leaven (i.e., delay it), but perform it immediately."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:58:05.939845651Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}